{
  "id": "COMPOUND:28340 - PROTEIN:5845",
  "verbalization": "Acodontasteroside D is shown to have a target relationship with SNU1 through multiple pathways, with the core mechanism involving the inhibition of a complex glycosylated compound, (1S,4S,5R,8R,10S,13R,14R,16R,17S,18R)-10,16-dihydroxy-4,5,9,9,13,20,20-heptamethyl-24-oxahexacyclo[15.5.2.01,18.04,17.05,14.08,13]tetracosan-23-one. This compound is identified as the target of both Acodontasteroside D and Prostate cells, which in turn target SNU1. The evidence suggests that Acodontasteroside D may act through a mechanism that affects the expression or function of this complex compound in prostate cells, leading to a downstream effect on SNU1. The consistent targeting of SNU1 across different pathways implies a potential role for Acodontasteroside D in modulating the activity of this compound, possibly through a direct or indirect interaction. The presence of a well-defined target relationship and the shared involvement of the compound in multiple pathways support the hypothesis that Acodontasteroside D may influence SNU1 via a mechanism involving the regulation of this complex glycosylated compound.",
